    'assets/js/ss-engine-thomas.js' => ['signals' => ['html-sink', 'remote-url'], 'reviewer' => 'SS-1361', 'review' => 'REMOTE-URL, and this is the one that matters: the engine sends an OUTBOUND REQUEST OFF-SITE from every public page. new Image().src to https://snapsmack.ca/releases/thomas-ping.php (:52-54), carrying a 32-hex uid, a type flag and a first-session flag. It counts how often the hidden bear is found. The uid comes from core/thomas-uid.php and is a random per-install value, never the site URL or name, and the regex at :44-45 strips it to 32 hex characters before use, so nothing else can ride in it. No page content, no visitor identifier and no site identity leave the browser. It is an img GET, which the public CSP img-src allows. ACCEPTED, with the point recorded plainly: this is telemetry to the vendor from every reader page on the fleet, it is the only asset in the library that ISSUES an off-site request, and whether a photoblog phones home at all is an owner decision rather than a code one. Four other assets carry the remote-url signal without making a request -- fjGallery, shortcode-toolbar, smack-qr and ss-pixel -- where the match is a licence or header citation, a placeholder, or a data: URI; each is reviewed separately as making no remote request. The distinction is deliberate: the signal finds candidate strings, the review decides which of them actually reach the network, and only this one does. HTML-SINK: three innerHTML writes. Two are entirely literal markup (:138 the dedication panel, :191 the caption). The third (:95) interpolates baseUrl, derived from this engine own script src via scripts[i].src.replace (:87-90) -- a same-origin URL the document already loaded, not page content and not user input; anybody able to set that src already has script execution. ALSO READ, no signal raised: sessionStorage ss_thomas (:48-49) holds the literal string 1 and nothing else, marking whether this session already found the bear so a repeat is not double-counted. No identifier, no user content, wrapped in try/catch.'],
    'assets/js/ss-engine-tile-like.js' => ['signals' => ['network'], 'reviewer' => 'SS-1323', 'review' => 'Reviewed the single call: a root-relative same-origin POST to /process-like.php carrying only an integer id, which is the endpoint and spelling the community dock already uses. IT ALSO SENDS A CSRF TOKEN WHEN THE PAGE CARRIES ONE, AND THAT BUYS NOTHING TODAY: process-like.php does not validate a token (the dock posts without one either). Saying the request carries a token, with no note that nothing checks it, reads as a protection that does not exist -- Muse flagged exactly that wording. The gap is pre-existing and is filed as SS-1385; this engine adds no new hole, because it is the same endpoint, the same table and the same rate limit. No DOM construction at all -- the engine toggles classes and ARIA attributes on markup the CMS rendered, so there is no html sink. Public CSP restricts connections to same-origin.'],
